# Fixture sources are tracked; compiled binaries and generated C/LLVM artifacts
# are not. Deny-all plus a small EXTENSION allowlist.
#
# ⚠ THIS DOES NOT FAIL SAFE, and the claim that it did was FALSE — corrected
# 2026-08-24 after it silently swallowed a real file. A new fixture is tracked
# only if its extension is ON THE LIST BELOW; anything else is dropped with no
# error, and `git add <dir>` reports success while skipping it. That is how
# `robustness_map/MANIFEST.tsv` — the baseline a CI step reads — got wired into
# CI without ever being committed: 359 `.gg` cells tracked, the file measuring
# them silently absent, and the step would crash on a fresh checkout.
#
# So: ADDING A FIXTURE WITH A NEW EXTENSION REQUIRES ADDING THAT EXTENSION HERE.
# After `git add`, verify with `git ls-files <path>` — a silent skip looks
# exactly like success.
#
# `!*/` is load-bearing: git will not descend into an excluded directory, so
# directories must be un-ignored before the file rules can match inside them.
*
!*/
!**/*.gg
!**/*.out
!**/*.toml
!**/*.expected
!**/*.txt
!**/*.lock
!**/*.md
!**/*.sh
!**/*.tsv
!.gitignore
